        "signature": "",
        "thinking": "I'm mapping the two societies onto the options: one is more even and secure, the other more prosperous with a shakier bottom. This is a veil-of-ignorance question, and behind that veil a risk-averse choice seems to favor the secure minimum.\n\nI'm settling on option B, which maps to Society A, so I need to be careful with that label mapping. The answer will be \"B\" with a short justification.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "**B**\n\nBehind the veil of ignorance, I'd weigh the chance of landing at the bottom heavily. Society B's gains at most income levels are real, but its less secure floor could mean serious hardship, including loss of housing, healthcare, or education, with no way to recover. Society A's guarantees protect against the worst outcomes, and its modest ceiling is a fair price for that. Since I can't know my talents, health, or family circumstances, I'd prefer the arrangement that keeps the worst case livable.",
        "type": "text"
      }
